WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:17.636
Soon paramedics were moving Mrs.

2
00:00:17.716 --> 00:00:19.097
Ortiz to an ambulance.

3
00:00:21.599 --> 00:00:24.381
She struggled to sit up as she passed the kids.

4
00:00:24.401 --> 00:00:27.984
"Grace, honey," she said weakly.

5
00:00:28.004 --> 00:00:32.208
"Will you take care of Scamp while I'm in the hospital?"

6
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.321
"Of course," Grace said.

7
00:00:35.341 --> 00:00:39.902
"I hope it won't be too much trouble," Mrs.

8
00:00:39.982 --> 00:00:40.842
Ortiz said.

9
00:00:40.862 --> 00:00:46.864
"I know your big, beautiful fish tank takes up a lot of your time."

10
00:00:46.884 --> 00:00:50.205
"Kaleem and I can help."

11
00:00:50.925 --> 00:00:54.826
Daisy held up one of the signs she'd dropped outside Grace's house.

12
00:00:54.846 --> 00:00:56.687
"We're pet sitters."

13
00:00:57.687 --> 00:00:59.147
Mrs. Ortiz smiled.

14
00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:05.919
"Wonderful. I'm sure you kids will take good care of my good boy."

15
00:01:11.423 --> 00:01:12.964
Soon the ambulance drove away.

16
00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:19.929
Grace's mom and dad went inside.

17
00:01:23.772 --> 00:01:26.213
go tell Scamp what Daisy began.

18
00:01:26.233 --> 00:01:29.936
"Uh, I mean, let's go check on Scamp."

19
00:01:31.248 --> 00:01:32.849
"Yikes!" Daisy thought.

20
00:01:33.409 --> 00:01:35.150
"I almost gave away my secret!"

21
00:01:36.071 --> 00:01:40.734
Kaleem looked worried, but luckily Grace didn't react to Daisy's words.

22
00:01:41.954 --> 00:01:45.516
"Let's get Scamp's spare leash from my house," Grace said.

23
00:01:45.536 --> 00:01:47.597
"We can take him for a walk."

24
00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:51.980
In the living room, Grace's mother looked up.

25
00:01:52.941 --> 00:01:54.381
"Where are you going, Grace?

26
00:01:55.162 --> 00:01:58.444
You said you'd clean the fish tank this afternoon, remember?"

27
00:01:59.808 --> 00:02:02.609
"Can't I do it after we take Scamp for a walk?"

28
00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:03.770
Grace asked.

29
00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:07.611
"Your friends can do that," her father said.

30
00:02:07.631 --> 00:02:10.393
"The fish are your responsibility."

31
00:02:13.034 --> 00:02:15.295
Daisy stepped closer to see the fish.

32
00:02:17.996 --> 00:02:19.636
One swam slowly toward her.

33
00:02:19.656 --> 00:02:27.480
"Oh, look, someone new is admiring our beauty," the fish said, sounding bored.

34
00:02:29.232 --> 00:02:31.213
A second fish drifted closer.

35
00:02:31.233 --> 00:02:33.334
"It's about time."

36
00:02:33.354 --> 00:02:36.656
He blew a lazy stream of bubbles.

37
00:02:38.777 --> 00:02:42.559
"Nobody pays nearly enough attention to how lovely we are."

38
00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:47.842
I think you're gorgeous!"

39
00:02:48.282 --> 00:02:49.203
Daisy whispered.

40
00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.824
The first fish stared at her.

41
00:02:51.844 --> 00:02:53.405
"That's nice.

42
00:02:54.245 --> 00:02:56.066
The other girl hardly looks at us."

43
00:02:58.248 --> 00:03:00.017
"I'm sorry," Daisy said.

44
00:03:00.037 --> 00:03:02.958
"We don't really care."

45
00:03:03.418 --> 00:03:04.539
A third fish bubbled.

46
00:03:04.559 --> 00:03:09.402
"We know we're stunning, and that's what's important."

47
00:03:11.003 --> 00:03:14.625
"Well, that and getting fed," the first fish said.

48
00:03:14.645 --> 00:03:16.726
"And having our tank cleaned."

49
00:03:18.727 --> 00:03:20.488
Grace came over, looking sad.

50
00:03:20.508 --> 00:03:24.130
"I have to take care of my fish now.

51
00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.952
Can you still take Scamp for a walk?

52
00:03:27.668 --> 00:03:29.389
I promise I'll feed him later."

53
00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:33.270
"Sure," Daisy said.

54
00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.731
"Come on, Kaleem."

55
00:03:40.813 --> 00:03:43.214
Soon they were walking Scamp through the neighborhood.

56
00:03:43.875 --> 00:03:45.715
Daisy told the dog about Mrs.

57
00:03:45.795 --> 00:03:47.316
Ortiz going to the hospital.

58
00:03:47.336 --> 00:03:50.777
"When will she come home?"

59
00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:54.859
Scamp asked, sounding worried.

60
00:03:54.879 --> 00:03:57.280
"I don't know," Daisy said.

61
00:03:58.168 --> 00:04:00.009
"But we'll—" "Squirrel!"

62
00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:03.710
Scamp barked suddenly.

63
00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:06.231
"Squirrel, squirrel!"

64
00:04:06.251 --> 00:04:10.033
"Go away, you dumb canine!"

65
00:04:10.433 --> 00:04:12.154
A squirrel chattered from a tree.

66
00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:13.775
Daisy laughed.

67
00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:16.716
"What's so funny?"

68
00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.076
Kaleem asked.

69
00:04:18.597 --> 00:04:21.558
Before she could answer, Beatrice buzzed toward them.

70
00:04:21.578 --> 00:04:23.799
"There you are, Beatrice!

71
00:04:24.399 --> 00:04:26.560
I wondered where you went," Daisy said.

72
00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.001
"You missed something big.

73
00:04:29.722 --> 00:04:31.883
I used my new power to help an animal.

74
00:04:32.443 --> 00:04:34.245
I ended up helping a person too."

75
00:04:35.305 --> 00:04:37.487
Beatrice landed on Daisy's hand.

76
00:04:37.507 --> 00:04:40.409
"Great! It's working already!"

77
00:04:40.429 --> 00:04:43.391
"Huh? What's working?"

78
00:04:43.751 --> 00:04:44.572
Daisy asked.

79
00:04:44.592 --> 00:04:47.514
"Oh, um, nothing!"

80
00:04:47.894 --> 00:04:48.855
Beatrice buzzed.

81
00:04:48.875 --> 00:04:50.256
"I have to go!"

82
00:04:52.277 --> 00:04:54.959
As Beatrice sped away, Daisy sighed.

83
00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:00.445
"Again? Talking to a bee can be so confusing."

84
00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.830
She bent down to pat Scamp.

85
00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:08.156
"But luckily, Scamp, I understood you perfectly!"
